{"deps":{"gaato/mttp":"0.2.0","gaato/zstd":"0.3.1","gaato/brotli":"0.4.1","gaato/deflate":"0.1.0","gaato/codec_bytes":"0.1.1"},"name":"gaato/mttp_async","readme":"README.md","source":"src","yanked":true,"license":"Apache-2.0","version":"0.1.0","checksum":"99b5908b726a9d1e5771b6ef02eaa4f3470936281be978d798790a4db89e213f","keywords":["http","client","server","retry","sse","async"],"created_at":"2026-11-12T03:48:12.252853+00:00","repository":"https://github.com/gaato/mttp","description":"HTTP for MoonBit apps that outgrow the built-in client: the module an app starts with, holding a ready client (retries with a budget, deadlines, redirects, cookies, decompression) and a server, on moonbitlang/core/async for native, wasm and js. Typed endpoints and OpenAPI come from gaato/mttp, which libraries depend on instead.","yanked_reason":"Renamed to gaato/mttp 0.3, the module an app adds; the I/O-free core is gaato/mttp_core. See https://github.com/gaato/mttp","preferred-target":"native","supported-targets":"native+wasm+js"}
